From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: cq8725s-ayn-odin3: deeper backlight floor

Steam's brightness slider stops at 40 on the 0..4096 luminance-linear
scale 0060 exposes, which is DBV ~411 through the driver's table: about
1% of full luminance, and still bright on the OLED in the dark. Override
the table for this board (0059's brightness-levels/num-interpolated-steps)
so the bottom quarter of Steam's slider spans DBV 12..968 log-evenly, and
everything from sysfs 256 up stays the driver's measured curve.

The floor, DBV 12 at sysfs 40, was picked on the device by stepping raw
DBV values: still visibly dimmer than ~118, and usable. Nothing in the
desktop session goes below 41 (hypridle's 1%) or 82 (swayosd's 2%), so
the steep 0..32 segment that interpolation leaves is never used.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts
@@ -233,6 +233,35 @@
 	pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
 
 	rotation = <90>;
+
+	/*
+	 * The driver's luminance-linear table (0060) with a deeper floor. Steam
+	 * never writes below 40 (it squares its slider, 1% of the scale), which
+	 * the driver's table puts at DBV ~411: still bright on an OLED at night.
+	 * Below the knee at 256 the DBV now falls log-evenly in Steam's slider
+	 * position to 12 at 40, the dimmest level judged usable on the device;
+	 * from 256 up these are the driver's entries unchanged.
+	 */
+	brightness-levels = <
+		   0    8   26   58  115  212  366  606
+		 968 1021 1072 1118 1164 1207 1248 1288
+		1327 1363 1399 1434 1468 1501 1533 1564
+		1595 1625 1654 1682 1711 1738 1765 1791
+		1817 1843 1868 1893 1917 1941 1965 1988
+		2011 2034 2056 2079 2101 2122 2143 2165
+		2186 2206 2226 2246 2266 2286 2306 2325
+		2344 2363 2381 2401 2419 2436 2455 2473
+		2491 2508 2526 2543 2561 2577 2594 2611
+		2627 2644 2661 2676 2693 2709 2725 2741
+		2756 2772 2787 2803 2818 2834 2849 2864
+		2879 2893 2908 2923 2937 2951 2966 2981
+		2995 3009 3023 3037 3051 3065 3078 3092
+		3106 3119 3133 3146 3160 3173 3186 3199
+		3212 3225 3238 3251 3264 3276 3289 3301
+		3315 3327 3340 3351 3364 3376 3389 3401
+		3413
+	>;
+	num-interpolated-steps = <32>;
 };
 
